**Statutory Scope & Clean Separation (*Lasercomb* & *WIREdata*):** Copyright permissions under this Section 2 govern expressive code and documentation of the Program (all copies of which are licensed, not sold under `17 U.S.C. § 117`). Copyright alone is not asserted to bar independent cleanroom implementation of uncopyrightable `17 U.S.C. § 102(b)` mathematical ideas after patent expiration or to claim copyright authorship over purely numerical solver outputs; rather, (a) copying and executing the Program in RAM/VRAM is scope-conditioned on your confining that execution to the Qualifying Open-Weights Field of Use, (b) practicing claimed apparatuses, `CRM` tensor structures, systems, and methods (including cleanroom re-implementations) is governed independently by Patent Rights under Section 11 during their statutory patent term, and (c) public Corresponding Source disclosure of Derived Model Weights is independently required as your bilateral contractual return performance under Section 9.

**Inference Outputs & Innocent-Host Scrape Protection:** End-user conversational text or SQL query result rows generated during compliant open-weights inference are not covered works. **Unauthorized scraping or downstream misuse of public inference outputs by an unrelated third party never terminates or impairs an innocent compliant licensee's grant; however, any party (or Corporate Affiliate) that generates, commissions, scrapes, or ingests outputs, trajectories, or scores from a covered work, dataset, or API bearing Appropriate Legal Notices to train, distill, fine-tune, filter, score, or align any model outside the Qualifying Open-Weights Field of Use acts without authorization, breaches the applicable API/dataset terms and Section 9, and triggers Section 0(2).**

**Internal Enterprise, Batch, & R&D Scope Condition:** You may load into RAM/VRAM, run, and propagate covered works privately **solely on the express condition precedent that BOTH (a) every base model involved is already a Qualifying Open-Weights Model, AND (b) all resulting Derived Model Weights (including transitive Section 0(2) downstream models) are publicly released as Corresponding Source under Section 6 prior to or contemporaneously with any commercial, production, internal-enterprise, employee/contractor tool use, offline batch, internal R&D benchmark, or model-training/distillation deployment** (permitting un-released local execution solely for transient, good-faith evaluation on an already-public Qualifying Open-Weights Model whose outputs, activations, and derived weights are promptly discarded and never entered into any proprietary product, service, or closed-weight pipeline). Contractors may run covered works solely on your behalf and under your liability for full compliance. Sublicensing is prohibited; Section 10 makes it unnecessary.

