- **b)** Carry prominent notices stating that it is released under This License (alongside any Permitted Upstream Open-Weights Community Terms applicable to an upstream base model).
- **c)** **Anti-Two-Step Laundering & Merged-Checkpoint Rule:** You must license the modified Program, **and make available every compiled weight cartridge, widened tensor delta, adapter, compilation manifest, and newly trained or distilled Derived Model Weight**, **under This License** (preserving all Open-Weights Corresponding Source, Patent Field-of-Use, and anti-laundering conditions intact, and **never** re-licensing cartridges, deltas, or Derived Model Weights under bare MIT/Apache-2.0 terms that permit downstream closed-weight capture). Where cartridges or widened tensors are mounted onto or statically merged into (`export-safetensors`) an upstream Qualifying Open-Weights Model, the upstream base tensors (and merged checkpoint) may simultaneously preserve and flow down that model's **Permitted Upstream Open-Weights Community Terms** (such as `Llama`, `Gemma`, `Qwen`, `DeepSeek`, or `NVIDIA Open Model License` attributions, AUPs, and `>= 100M MAU` thresholds), provided complete base and Derived Model Weights remain publicly downloadable free of charge under Section 6.
