You may not load, execute, propagate, modify, host, import, or serve a covered work (including Derived Model Weights) or practice Patent Rights except as expressly authorized within the Qualifying Open-Weights Field of Use. Any attempt otherwise to do so is unauthorized *ab initio*, void, and **automatically and immediately terminates all Copyright and patent rights granted to you and your Corporate Affiliates under this License, requiring your immediate deletion and destruction of all copies of the Program in your possession or control (`17 U.S.C. § 117`)**.

For good-faith, inadvertent technical omissions involving a model already publicly released as a Qualifying Open-Weights Model (such as a broken mirror link or omitted config file), curing the omission within 30 days of written notice reinstates your grant. **However, any use in connection with a closed-weight, internal-only, or proprietary model (including transitive Section 0(2) synthetic-data, verifier, or relay pipelines) falls wholly inside the Reserved Proprietary & Closed-Weights Field of Use, is NEVER eligible for automatic cure or reinstatement without an express written settlement and commercial license executed by Licensor, and cessation of use or checkpoint deletion never extinguishes liability for accrued Copyright infringement (`17 U.S.C. §§ 502–505`), pre-issuance provisional patent royalties upon publication (`35 U.S.C. § 154(d)`), patent infringement upon issuance (`35 U.S.C. §§ 271, 283–285`, including enhanced treble damages for willful infringement), breach of contract, or unjust enrichment.**

**Factual Basis for Irreparable Harm, Specific Performance (`SFC v. Vizio`), & `Rule 65(c)` Security:** Closed-weight compilation, distillation, or deployment irreversibly transfers un-recoverable structural capability into proprietary checkpoints while eroding open-weights parity and Licensor's commercial licensing market in ways incapable of retrospective monetary calculation. Accordingly, you stipulate as a matter of fact that unauthorized closed-weight use or non-disclosure of Derived Model Weights renders monetary damages alone inadequate, supporting temporary, preliminary, and permanent injunctive relief, impoundment, and **equitable specific performance compelling Corresponding Source disclosure** (*Software Freedom Conservancy v. Vizio*)—**without bond, or where security is required under `Fed. R. Civ. P. 65(c)` or applicable law, upon posting a nominal bond not to exceed `$1,000`**—in addition to statutory/actual damages, disgorgement, reasonable royalties, and statutory attorneys' fees (`17 U.S.C. § 505`; `35 U.S.C. § 285`).

